WEBVTT
Language: en

seg-001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Hello! Today we learn our
first Python variable.

seg-002
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:14.500
This lesson takes only three minutes.

seg-003
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:24.500
A variable is a name we give to a value.

seg-004
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:35.000
It is like a label stuck on a box.

seg-005
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.000
The box holds a value
and the label is the name.

seg-005-2
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
When the computer sees the name,
it remembers the value inside.

seg-006
00:00:50.500 --> 00:01:00.000
Now let's write it. First the name: age.

seg-007
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
[keyboard typing]
Then the equals sign,
then the value: twenty-four.

seg-008
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:25.000
So age means twenty-four. Because it
is a number, it is called an integer.

seg-009
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:45.000
Now let's see the value. We write print
and, in brackets, the name: age.

seg-010
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Let's run the program.

seg-011
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.000
We can also store a name in a variable.

seg-011-2
00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.000
Text goes inside quotation marks;
this is called a string.

seg-012
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
A variable name must not start
with a number or contain spaces.

seg-012-2
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Capital and small letters are different.

seg-013
00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:41.500
In short: a variable
is a name for a value.

seg-013-2
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:47.500
age = 24 stores the value,
and print shows it.

seg-014
00:02:50.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Now one question: what does age = 24 do?
